// spec: std §3.2.5
// needs: threads net
// expect-exit: 0
// expect-stdout:
// clean: ok pong
// expired: Certificate alert 45: certificate expired or not yet valid
// not yet valid: Certificate alert 45: certificate expired or not yet valid
// no serverAuth: Certificate alert 43: certificate not valid for server authentication
// wrong name: Certificate alert 42: certificate is not valid for localhost
// bad signature: Certificate alert 42: bad certificate signature
// unknown CA: Certificate alert 48: certificate signed by an unknown authority
// unknown EE extension: Protocol alert 110: unexpected extension 4660 in EncryptedExtensions
// server_name with data: Protocol alert 47: server_name acknowledged wrongly
// unknown ServerHello extension: Protocol alert 110: unexpected extension 4660 in ServerHello
// unrequested SCT: Protocol alert 110: unexpected extension 18 in Certificate
// bad CertificateVerify: Protocol alert 51: bad CertificateVerify signature
// bad Finished: Protocol alert 51: bad server Finished
// KeyUpdate 2: read: tls: malformed KeyUpdate
// post-handshake type 99: read: tls: unexpected post-handshake message 99
// HRR for a group already sent: Protocol alert 47: HelloRetryRequest for an unusable group
// 16 MiB post-handshake message: read: tls: handshake message too long
// failed handshake: record 21 alert 50, then closed: true
// mutated server flights: 24, forged CertificateVerify / Finished accepted: 0, under 5 s each: true
// mutated client flights: 24, forged CertificateVerify / Finished accepted: 0, under 5 s each: true
// mutated ClientHellos: 48, under 5 s each: true
// mutated server flights (plaintext): 40, under 5 s each: true
// mutated DER / PEM: 900, hostile DER rejected: 12 of 12

// TLS against hostile peers and inputs: an alert, never a panic or a hang.
use rok::core::convert::AsBytes;
use rok::std::net::{tcp_listen, tcp_connect, TcpStream, Shutdown};
use rok::std::net::tls::{Client, Server, ClientConfig, ServerConfig, Certificate, PrivateKey, CipherSuite};
